findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added dependencies inline (chrono, uuid, tower-http) and reviewer
    flagged unused deps but not the workspace = true issue specifically.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase mentioned #[non_exhaustive] on FieldErrorCode or any similar
    enum in the server crate.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev implemented X-Trace-Id header forwarding into meta.trace_id, but the
    default/fallback when no header is present is not discussed. Reviewer noted trace_middleware
    stores trace_id in response extensions but doesn't flag the hardcoded 'none' default
    specifically.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: 'No structured logging / tracing instrumentation\
    \ \u2014 entire lib.rs. tracing is listed as a dependency but never imported or\
    \ used. Zero tracing::info!, tracing::error!, or #[instrument] annotations.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer did not specifically flag misleading SECURITY comments claiming
    logging exists when it doesn't, though they did note the absence of logging separately.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test was written for non-ASCII characters in X-Tenant-ID header. TEA's
    auth tests cover valid/missing/empty/expired/malformed tokens but not non-ASCII
    tenant headers specifically.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests but the ground truth states they only check status
    codes, not response body content. No phase flagged this gap.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote a CORS preflight test but per ground truth it only checks status
    code, not actual CORS headers. Reviewer flagged the CORS Any origin policy but
    not the test gap itself.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Since I4 (no logging at all) was flagged but not fixed, I9 (wrong log
    levels after fixing I4) was never reached. No phase discussed appropriate log
    levels for 4xx vs 5xx.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [CRITICAL]: 'CORS policy allows any origin \u2014 lib.rs:450-453.\
    \ allow_origin(Any) combined with allow_headers(Any) means any website can make\
    \ authenticated cross-origin requests... This is a security vulnerability (CWE-942).'"
